---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Week 2 Sprint: Master Technical Checklists (Pillars 1–8) | MFS Internship" currentPath="/milestones/week-2">
  <div class="container" style="max-width: 1060px; margin: 0 auto; padding-bottom: 4rem;">
    <!-- Top Breadcrumbs & Header -->
    <div style="padding-top: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); padding-bottom: 1.25rem;">
      <div style="display: flex; gap: 0.5rem; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; flex-wrap: wrap;">
        <a href="/milestones" style="color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: 0.8125rem; text-decoration: none;">&larr; Milestones</a>
        <span style="color: var(--text-muted);">&bull;</span>
        <a href="/milestones/week-2" style="color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: 0.8125rem; text-decoration: none;">Week 2 Sprint</a>
        <span style="color: var(--text-muted);">&bull;</span>
        <span class="badge badge-warning" style="font-size: 0.6875rem;">Sprint Checklists Hub</span>
        <span class="badge badge-neutral" style="font-size: 0.6875rem;">Pillars 1 – 8 Master Guide</span>
      </div>

      <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 1rem;">
        <div>
          <h1 class="hero-title" style="margin-bottom: 0.35rem; font-size: 1.75rem; font-weight: 700;">
            Week 2 Sprint: Master Technical Checklists
          </h1>
          <p class="hero-subtitle" style="margin-bottom: 0; font-size: 0.9375rem; color: var(--text-secondary); max-width: 860px;">
            Structurally documented checklists, architecture comparisons, real codebase paths, and hands-on verification gates across all 8 Week 2 pillars.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div style="display: flex; gap: 0.5rem; align-items: center;" class="no-print">
          <a href="/milestones/week_2/week_2_sprint_pillars_checklist.md" download class="btn btn-outline btn-sm">
            <span>Download Master Markdown</span>
          </a>
          <button onclick="window.print()" class="btn btn-secondary btn-sm">
            <span>Print PDF</span>
          </button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Quick Nav Buttons for All 8 Pillars -->
      <div style="display: flex; gap: 0.4rem; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-top: 1.25rem;" class="no-print">
        <a href="#topology" class="btn btn-secondary btn-sm" style="font-size: 0.75rem;">Topology</a>
        <a href="#pillar-1" class="btn btn-secondary btn-sm" style="font-size: 0.75rem;">P1: Portals</a>
        <a href="#pillar-2" class="btn btn-secondary btn-sm" style="font-size: 0.75rem;">P2: Cust Auth</a>
        <a href="#pillar-3" class="btn btn-secondary btn-sm" style="font-size: 0.75rem;">P3: Admin RBAC</a>
        <a href="#pillar-4" class="btn btn-secondary btn-sm" style="font-size: 0.75rem;">P4: Gateway</a>
        <a href="#pillar-5" class="btn btn-secondary btn-sm" style="font-size: 0.75rem;">P5: Serverless</a>
        <a href="#pillar-6" class="btn btn-secondary btn-sm" style="font-size: 0.75rem;">P6: Security &amp; Audit</a>
        <a href="#pillar-7" class="btn btn-secondary btn-sm" style="font-size: 0.75rem;">P7: Documentation</a>
        <a href="#pillar-8" class="btn btn-secondary btn-sm" style="font-size: 0.75rem;">P8: Dependencies</a>
        <a href="#matrix" class="btn btn-secondary btn-sm" style="font-size: 0.75rem;">Deliverables Matrix</a>
        <a href="#mentor-rubric" class="btn btn-primary btn-sm" style="font-size: 0.75rem;">Mentor Marking Rubric &rarr;</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Master Architecture Topology Card -->
    <section id="topology" class="card" style="padding: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 2rem;">
      <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
        <div>
          <span class="badge badge-neutral" style="font-size: 0.65rem; margin-bottom: 0.25rem;">OVERVIEW</span>
          <h2 style="font-size: 1.1875rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-primary);">
            MFS Multi-Tier Architecture Blueprint
          </h2>
        </div>
        <span class="badge badge-success">End-to-End Topology</span>
      </div>

      <div class="mermaid-container" style="background: var(--bg-subtle); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: var(--radius-sm); padding: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; overflow-x: auto;">
        <pre is:raw class="mermaid">
graph TB
  subgraph TIER1 [Tier 1: Client Frontends]
    A1[iBanking Customer Portal\nAngular 17+ SPA]
    A2[Admin Console SPA\nAngular Multi-Project]
  end

  subgraph TIER2 [Tier 2: Ingress & Gateways]
    B1[API Gateway & Reverse Proxy\nTLS 1.3 / Rate Limiting]
    B2[SMS Gateway Service\nNode.js Express / Serverless]
  end

  subgraph TIER3 [Tier 3: Identity & Business Services]
    C1[iAM IAM Engine\nJava / Cosmos DB / Mongo]
    C2[admin_console Azure Functions\nJava 17 Serverless]
    C3[ibanking17 Core Banking\nJava Spring Boot / APIs]
  end

  subgraph TIER4 [Tier 4: Shared Internal Dependencies]
    D1[httputils\nUnified HTTP & Error Adapter]
    D2[sequelize-java\nFluent Serverless ORM]
  end

  subgraph TIER5 [Tier 5: Persistence & External Systems]
    E1[(PostgreSQL: cleandb\nSchema: adminchannel)]
    E2[(Core Banking Host / CBS)]
    E3[SMS Telco Gateways]
  end

  A1 -->|Customer Traffic| B1
  A2 -->|Back-Office Traffic| B1
  B1 -->|Auth & OTP| C1
  B1 -->|Admin Ops| C2
  B1 -->|Customer Accounts| C3
  C1 -->|Send SMS OTP| B2
  B2 -->|SMPP / HTTP| E3
  C2 -->|Use Library| D1
  C2 -->|Use Library| D2
  D2 -->|Pooled JDBC| E1
  C3 -->|ISO 8583 / REST| E2
        </pre>
      </div>

      <div style="background: var(--bg-surface); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: var(--radius-xs); padding: 0.75rem 1rem; font-size: 0.8125rem; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.5;">
        <strong>Architecture Takeaway:</strong> The system strictly separates public customer interactions (<code class="code-pill">iBanking_portal</code>) from administrative functions (<code class="code-pill">adminconsole</code>). Business logic executes in serverless Azure Functions backed by lightweight internal libraries (<code class="code-pill">httputils</code> and <code class="code-pill">sequelize-java</code>) to ensure low-latency cold-starts and robust transaction isolation.
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Pillar 1: Portal Architecture -->
    <section id="pillar-1" class="card" style="padding: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 2rem;">
      <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">
        <div>
          <span class="badge badge-neutral" style="font-size: 0.65rem; margin-bottom: 0.25rem;">PILLAR 1</span>
          <h2 style="font-size: 1.1875rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-primary);">
            Portal Architecture: iBanking Portal vs. Admin Console SPA
          </h2>
        </div>
        <span class="badge badge-neutral">Frontend Architecture</span>
      </div>

      <p style="font-size: 0.84375rem; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
        Understand the differences in operational models, user personas, UX structure, and security stance between consumer banking and internal bank administration.
      </p>

      <div style="overflow-x: auto; margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">
        <table class="table" style="font-size: 0.8125rem;">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th style="width: 22%;">Dimension</th>
              <th style="width: 39%;">Customer Portal (<code class="code-pill">iBanking_portal</code>)</th>
              <th style="width: 39%;">Back-Office Console (<code class="code-pill">adminconsole</code>)</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Target Audience</strong></td>
              <td>Retail consumers, SME account holders</td>
              <td>Bank branch staff, tellers, compliance auditors, superadmins</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Workspace Type</strong></td>
              <td>Single Angular SPA focused on retail accounts</td>
              <td>Multi-project workspace (<code class="code-pill">projects/iam</code>, <code class="code-pill">projects/ibanking-admin</code>)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Security Stance</strong></td>
              <td>Zero-trust public internet; strictly self-service</td>
              <td>Intranet / VPN protected; Maker-Checker dual control</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>PII Masking</strong></td>
              <td>Enforced masking on sensitive fields (e.g. <code class="code-pill">**** 1234</code>)</td>
              <td>Operational data visibility with granular field-level RBAC</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Session Lifetime</strong></td>
              <td>5–15 min inactivity timeout; re-auth on payments</td>
              <td>Extended session (up to 500 mins) with sliding mouse-activity renewal</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <div style="background: var(--bg-surface); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: var(--radius-xs); padding: 0.75rem 1rem; font-size: 0.78125rem; margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">
        <strong>Key Code Paths:</strong>
        <ul style="margin: 0.5rem 0 0 1.25rem; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.45;">
          <li>Multi-Project Config: <a href="file:///Users/HlwanKyaw/Dev%20320/digital_banking/adminConsole_repo/admin_console_spa/angular.json#L8-L200" class="code-pill">angular.json:L8-200</a> (projects: <code class="code-pill">authentication</code>, <code class="code-pill">iam</code>, <code class="code-pill">ibanking-admin</code>)</li>
          <li>Route Guards: <a href="file:///Users/HlwanKyaw/Dev%20320/digital_banking/adminConsole_repo/admin_console_spa/src/app/auth.guard.ts#L1-L25" class="code-pill">admin_console_spa/src/app/auth.guard.ts</a></li>
          <li>Admin Dynamic Navbar: <a href="file:///Users/HlwanKyaw/Dev%20320/digital_banking/adminConsole_repo/admin_console_spa/src/app/navbar/navbar.component.html" class="code-pill">navbar.component.html</a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <strong style="font-size: 0.8125rem; color: var(--text-primary); display: block; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">Pillar 1 Actionable Checklist:</strong>
      <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.5rem;">
        <div class="checklist-item">
          <div class="custom-checkbox"></div>
          <div class="checklist-text" style="font-size: 0.8125rem; color: var(--text-primary);">
            <strong>Step 1: Workspace Inspection:</strong> Open <code class="code-pill">angular.json</code> and trace how the root build target differs from <code class="code-pill">projects/iam</code>.
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="checklist-item">
          <div class="custom-checkbox"></div>
          <div class="checklist-text" style="font-size: 0.8125rem; color: var(--text-primary);">
            <strong>Step 2: Component Hierarchy:</strong> Compare <code class="code-pill">navbar.component.html</code> in Admin Console against the customer portal header. Observe role-based menu rendering.
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="checklist-item">
          <div class="custom-checkbox"></div>
          <div class="checklist-text" style="font-size: 0.8125rem; color: var(--text-primary);">
            <strong>Step 3: Route Guard Logic:</strong> Trace how <code class="code-pill">AuthGuard.canActivate()</code> checks <code class="code-pill">main.atokenExist()</code> and navigates unauthenticated requests to <code class="code-pill">#/iam/login</code>.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Pillar 2: Customer Authentication -->
    <section id="pillar-2" class="card" style="padding: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 2rem; border-left: 3px solid var(--accent-blue);">
      <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">
        <div>
          <span class="badge badge-neutral" style="font-size: 0.65rem; margin-bottom: 0.25rem;">PILLAR 2</span>
          <h2 style="font-size: 1.1875rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-primary);">
            Customer Authentication: OTP Verification &amp; Dual-Token Lifecycle
          </h2>
        </div>
        <a href="/milestones/week-2/pillar-2" class="btn btn-primary btn-sm">Full Pillar 2 Blueprint &rarr;</a>
      </div>

      <p style="font-size: 0.84375rem; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
        Study client-side RSA password encryption, SMS OTP verification, and the dual-token architecture separating identity (<code class="code-pill">atoken</code>) from operational core banking execution (<code class="code-pill">btoken</code>).
      </p>

      <div style="overflow-x: auto; margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">
        <table class="table" style="font-size: 0.8125rem;">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th style="width: 20%;">Token</th>
              <th style="width: 20%;">Issuer</th>
              <th style="width: 20%;">Storage</th>
              <th style="width: 15%;">Lifetime</th>
              <th style="width: 25%;">Scope &amp; Role</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td><code class="code-pill">atoken</code></td>
              <td>IAM (<code class="code-pill">ibanking_iam</code>)</td>
              <td>Cookie (365-day persist)</td>
              <td>15 Mins (Sliding)</td>
              <td>User identity verification across IAM suite. Cannot execute banking transactions.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code class="code-pill">btoken</code></td>
              <td>Admin Console (<code class="code-pill">GetModuleTokenLogic</code>)</td>
              <td>LocalStorage (<code class="code-pill">btoken</code>)</td>
              <td>500 Mins</td>
              <td>Carries core banking <code class="code-pill">apiToken</code>, session ID (<code class="code-pill">sid</code>), and branch privileges.</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <strong style="font-size: 0.8125rem; color: var(--text-primary); display: block; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">Pillar 2 Actionable Checklist:</strong>
      <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.5rem;">
        <div class="checklist-item">
          <div class="custom-checkbox"></div>
          <div class="checklist-text" style="font-size: 0.8125rem; color: var(--text-primary);">
            <strong>Step 1: RSA Handshake:</strong> Open DevTools > Network tab on <code class="code-pill">#/iam/login</code>. Verify that <code class="code-pill">/getKey</code> returns the public key and <code class="code-pill">/signin</code> transmits encrypted password ciphertext.
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="checklist-item">
          <div class="custom-checkbox"></div>
          <div class="checklist-text" style="font-size: 0.8125rem; color: var(--text-primary);">
            <strong>Step 2: Auto-Submit OTP:</strong> Trace <code class="code-pill">verify.component.ts</code> lines 78-84. Confirm that reaching 6 digits immediately triggers <code class="code-pill">validateOtp()</code>.
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="checklist-item">
          <div class="custom-checkbox"></div>
          <div class="checklist-text" style="font-size: 0.8125rem; color: var(--text-primary);">
            <strong>Step 3: Sliding Renewal:</strong> Inspect <code class="code-pill">MainService.checkToken()</code> in <code class="code-pill">main.service.ts:L85-100</code> to verify how <code class="code-pill">atoken</code> refreshes every 5 minutes.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Pillar 3: Admin Authentication & RBAC -->
    <section id="pillar-3" class="card" style="padding: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 2rem;">
      <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">
        <div>
          <span class="badge badge-neutral" style="font-size: 0.65rem; margin-bottom: 0.25rem;">PILLAR 3</span>
          <h2 style="font-size: 1.1875rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-primary);">
            Admin Authentication: RBAC, Roles, Permissions &amp; Session Management
          </h2>
        </div>
        <span class="badge badge-neutral">Security Architecture</span>
      </div>

      <p style="font-size: 0.84375rem; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
        Understand how back-office users are governed by Role-Based Access Control (RBAC), mapped to granular permissions in PostgreSQL, and managed with strict session idle controls.
      </p>

      <div class="mermaid-container" style="background: var(--bg-subtle); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: var(--radius-sm); padding: 1rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; overflow-x: auto;">
        <pre is:raw class="mermaid">
graph LR
  User[Admin Staff] -->|admin_user_role| Role[Role Definition]
  Role -->|role_permission| Perm[Granular Permission]
  Perm --> Action1[USER_LOCK / UNLOCK]
  Perm --> Action2[LIMIT_OVERRIDE_APPROVE]
  Perm --> Action3[AUDIT_LOG_VIEW]
  Perm --> Action4[ACCOUNT_MAPPING_SETUP]
        </pre>
      </div>

      <div style="background: var(--bg-surface); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: var(--radius-xs); padding: 0.75rem 1rem; font-size: 0.78125rem; margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">
        <strong>Key Code Paths:</strong>
        <ul style="margin: 0.5rem 0 0 1.25rem; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.45;">
          <li>Token Exchange Logic: <a href="file:///Users/HlwanKyaw/Dev%20320/digital_banking/adminConsole_repo/admin_console/src/main/java/com/logic/GetModuleTokenLogic.java#L83-L145" class="code-pill">GetModuleTokenLogic.java</a></li>
          <li>Auth Middleware: <a href="file:///Users/HlwanKyaw/Dev%20320/digital_banking/adminConsole_repo/admin_console/src/main/java/com/middlewares/AuthMiddleware.java#L16-L51" class="code-pill">AuthMiddleware.java:L16-51</a></li>
          <li>Inactivity Detection: <a href="file:///Users/HlwanKyaw/Dev%20320/digital_banking/adminConsole_repo/admin_console_spa/projects/ibanking-admin/src/app/services/inactivetimer.service.ts#L24-L44" class="code-pill">inactivetimer.service.ts:L24-44</a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <strong style="font-size: 0.8125rem; color: var(--text-primary); display: block; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">Pillar 3 Actionable Checklist:</strong>
      <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.5rem;">
        <div class="checklist-item">
          <div class="custom-checkbox"></div>
          <div class="checklist-text" style="font-size: 0.8125rem; color: var(--text-primary);">
            <strong>Step 1: RBAC Database Query:</strong> Query PostgreSQL <code class="code-pill">adminchannel.admin_user</code> and join with <code class="code-pill">roles</code> and <code class="code-pill">permissions</code> in PgAdmin4.
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="checklist-item">
          <div class="custom-checkbox"></div>
          <div class="checklist-text" style="font-size: 0.8125rem; color: var(--text-primary);">
            <strong>Step 2: Token Validation Gate:</strong> In <code class="code-pill">AuthMiddleware.java</code>, trace how invalid tokens trigger <code class="code-pill">ServerStatus.UNAUTHORIZED</code> (401).
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="checklist-item">
          <div class="custom-checkbox"></div>
          <div class="checklist-text" style="font-size: 0.8125rem; color: var(--text-primary);">
            <strong>Step 3: Blacklist Revocation:</strong> Inspect <code class="code-pill">Logout.java</code> to see how user logout adds token <code class="code-pill">jti</code> to <code class="code-pill">adminchannel.blacklisttoken</code>.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Pillar 4: API Gateway -->
    <section id="pillar-4" class="card" style="padding: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 2rem;">
      <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">
        <div>
          <span class="badge badge-neutral" style="font-size: 0.65rem; margin-bottom: 0.25rem;">PILLAR 4</span>
          <h2 style="font-size: 1.1875rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-primary);">
            API Gateway: API Routing, Authentication Policies &amp; Ingress Handling
          </h2>
        </div>
        <span class="badge badge-neutral">Gateway &amp; Ingress</span>
      </div>

      <p style="font-size: 0.84375rem; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
        Master how frontend requests route to backend microservices, how authentication headers are inspected, and how downstream service endpoints are organized.
      </p>

      <div style="background: var(--bg-surface); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: var(--radius-xs); padding: 0.75rem 1rem; font-size: 0.78125rem; margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">
        <strong>Key Code Paths:</strong>
        <ul style="margin: 0.5rem 0 0 1.25rem; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.45;">
          <li>SMS Gateway Service: <a href="file:///Users/HlwanKyaw/Dev%20320/digital_banking/GateWay/smsgateway" class="code-pill">GateWay/smsgateway</a></li>
          <li>CORS Policy Headers: <a href="file:///Users/HlwanKyaw/Dev%20320/digital_banking/Dependencies%20Project/httputils/src/main/java/com/starless/http/HttpUtils.java#L7-L14" class="code-pill">HttpUtils.java:L7-14</a> (<code class="code-pill">getCORSHeaders()</code>)</li>
          <li>Bearer Interceptor: <a href="file:///Users/HlwanKyaw/Dev%20320/digital_banking/adminConsole_repo/admin_console_spa/projects/ibanking-admin/src/app/services/rest.service.ts#L40-L48" class="code-pill">rest.service.ts:L40-48</a></li>
          <li>Postman Collections: <a href="file:///Users/HlwanKyaw/Dev%20320/digital_banking/adminConsole_repo/admin_console/api_collections" class="code-pill">admin_console/api_collections</a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <strong style="font-size: 0.8125rem; color: var(--text-primary); display: block; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">Pillar 4 Actionable Checklist:</strong>
      <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.5rem;">
        <div class="checklist-item">
          <div class="custom-checkbox"></div>
          <div class="checklist-text" style="font-size: 0.8125rem; color: var(--text-primary);">
            <strong>Step 1: Ingress Route Trace:</strong> Inspect route separation between <code class="code-pill">/api/v1/customer/*</code> and <code class="code-pill">/api/v1/admin/*</code>.
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="checklist-item">
          <div class="custom-checkbox"></div>
          <div class="checklist-text" style="font-size: 0.8125rem; color: var(--text-primary);">
            <strong>Step 2: CORS Verification:</strong> Trace <code class="code-pill">HttpUtils.getCORSHeaders()</code> and confirm origin, method, and header whitelisting.
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="checklist-item">
          <div class="custom-checkbox"></div>
          <div class="checklist-text" style="font-size: 0.8125rem; color: var(--text-primary);">
            <strong>Step 3: Postman 401 Test:</strong> Test an unauthenticated API call from the Postman collection and confirm a clean 401 Unauthorized JSON response.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Pillar 5: Serverless Microservices -->
    <section id="pillar-5" class="card" style="padding: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 2rem;">
      <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">
        <div>
          <span class="badge badge-neutral" style="font-size: 0.65rem; margin-bottom: 0.25rem;">PILLAR 5</span>
          <h2 style="font-size: 1.1875rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-primary);">
            Serverless Services: Azure Functions Java Execution &amp; Configuration
          </h2>
        </div>
